# Ratchet allowlist for the patterns gate (scripts/qa-patterns.bash, src-go/qa/patterns).
#
# semgrep's bash grammar (tree-sitter-bash) stops at some valid bash and then sees none of the
# rest of the file, so no rule can judge it. A shell file with more than half of its lines
# outside the parse tree fails the gate unless it is listed here. Rows:
#
#   <path> TAB <lines outside the parse tree> TAB <the construct that stops the parser>
#
# A record may only be lowered: the gate fails when the file is above its record (it grew),
# below it (lower the number) or no longer mostly unparsed (delete the row). Never add a row
# for a new file: rewrite the construct in equivalent bash the grammar reads.
